Of course you can look at it. Yeah, I want your opinion too.

56
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:56,650
- Okay. - Here you go.

57
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:59,400
- What do you think about centerpieces?     - Centerpieces.

58
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:02,650
- Roses or lilies?     - Definitely roses.

59
00:04:06,990 --> 00:04:10,330
Well, I just think they're a bit more wedding-y, you know.

60
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:16,000
- But lilies are the clear choice.     - Oh, my God, it's like one mind.

61
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:17,670
Uh-huh.

62
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:21,920
Guys, guys, you gotta let me nap.

63
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,680
I'm gonna get cranky.

64
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:29,050
Joey, there is a perfectly good couch across the hall.

65
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,560
Yes, it is perfectly good...

66
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:35,270
...and it is not one of the places the duck got sick.

67
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:37,350
What?

68
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:41,860
- All right, I'm gonna go.     - Joey, what did the duck do?

69
00:04:42,150 --> 00:04:45,070
I don't know, but he did not eat your face cream.

70
00:04:56,870 --> 00:04:57,920
Hey, little buddy.

71
00:04:59,290 --> 00:05:01,250
How you feeling? Aah.

72
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:06,170
What the hell is in that face cream?

73
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:21,980
That's so soft.

74
00:05:24,570 --> 00:05:26,780
Pillowcases.

75
00:05:29,570 --> 00:05:31,910
Oh, ah.

76
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:46,300
"Zelda looked at the chimney sweep. Her father, the vicar..."

77
00:05:46,590 --> 00:05:47,840
Vicar?

78
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,430
"...wouldn't be home for hours.

79
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:53,600
Her loins were burning.

80
00:05:53,810 --> 00:05:58,020
She threw caution to the wind and reached out and grabbed his..."

81
